      <description>[rɛ:p] Quotation: Dh’fhàg e [rɛ:p] sios air a’ bhroilleach. Notes: untidy mess on clothes.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp166276544">tòtaman</headword>
      <description>[ṯɔ:ṯɑ̃mɑṉ] Notes: a spinning top.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp166278272">cart</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Cart na cosgais. Notes: (Uist) the cart which contained the spirits, biscuits and cheese, and tobacco, and which followed the remains at a funeral. [NOTES: slipped under ‘cairt na cosgais’.]</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp166280072">dànas</headword>
      <description>Quotation: “Nach ann ort a tha ’n dànas.” Notes: sport, diversion.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp166281728">déile-bhogadain</headword>
      <description>[dʹɤıləvoɡəd̪ɑ̃nʹ] Notes: see-saw.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp166283456">dóite</headword>
      <description>[d̪o:tʹə] Notes: bare, without anything.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp166285184">[ɡɑ̃:]</headword>
      <description>Quotation: [ɡɑ̃:] ris an fhardaich. Notes: in the immediate vicinity of the house.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
